{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":32},"timestamp":1793490650,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":"bash /home/claude/solves/narnia/L2.sh","title":"Narnia L2 -> narnia3: buf[128] strcpy overflow, shellcode assembled with nasm","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/bash"}}
[0.003, "o", "$ ssh narnia2@narnia.labs.overthewire.org -p 2226   # password 0h8Tj5fxbv\r\n$ cat /narnia/narnia2.c   # char buf[128]; strcpy(buf, argv[1]);\r\n$ objdump: sub $0x80,%esp; strcpy@plt -> buffer at ebp-0x80, ret at offset 132\r\n$ readelf: GNU_STACK RWE -> the stack is executable\r\n$ write /tmp/l2.asm in the shell, nasm -f elf32, objdump the object,\r\n$ objcopy -O binary --only-section=.text -> raw bytes, xxd them\r\n$ then python3 the exploit: NOP sled + shellcode + saved ebp + return address\r\n$   sweeping 0xffffd000..0xffffe800, detecting the PWN! marker\r\n"]
